# Multi-modal communication through utterance and potentially expressions, gestures, etc. .

std_skills/Meta meta

# The ID of the person to interact with.
# If empty, any user can be interacted with.
string person_id

# The ID of the group of persons to interact with.
# If empty, any group of persons can be interacted with.
# If not empty, the 'person_id' field should be ignored.
string group_id

# The text to be uttered.
# It might contains additional markup for multi-modal communication.
# See the documentation at
# https://gitlab.pal-robotics.com/interaction/communication_hub/-/blob/main/doc/multi_modal_expression_markup_language.md
string input

---
std_skills/Result result

---
std_skills/Feedback feedback

# Vizij's extension to the standard, proposed to ROS4HRI (see the
# "Departures from upstream" table in arora-msgs-ros2's README): the mouth
# shape the utterance is making as it plays, for a client that mirrors the
# lips or captions the speech. One of the 15 industry viseme shapes
# (sil PP FF TH DD kk CH SS nn RR aa E ih oh ou), `sil` when the mouth is at
# rest. Streamed as each viseme is reached, never ahead of the audio.
string viseme

# How strongly the shape is driven, [0, 1] — 0 with `sil`.
float32 intensity
